.*/
!projects/**/.vscode/

tmp.*
tmp/
#data/	# ./data is a submodule
logs/
output*/

# Audit worklists: large, fully regenerated by ./run-audit on every run, and
# derivable from the dataset. The report itself stays tracked -- keeping its
# filename stable is what makes `git diff` between runs readable.
project/reports/*.csv

# Generated audit reports. They describe the *library* -- trip-by-trip counts,
# folder names -- not the software, and ./tool-audit and ./tool-dedup rewrite
# them on every run. Tracking them published a travel history and meant a run
# dirtied the tree. Hand-written analysis (species_discovery_report.md) stays.
project/reports/data_preview_report.md
project/reports/sidecar_dedup_report.md
project/reports/label_run_audit.md
project/reports/wraparound_split_report.md
project/reports/archive/
#results/
**/.env

# Your machines' host names. `_config.local.toml` is the tracked template.
config.local.toml

# Period-specific working files: ad-hoc run commands for whatever is being
# tried this week, and manifests that name real trips. Neither is permanent or
# shareable, and the manifests would publish a travel history. Scripts here
# should start with `cd "$(dirname "$0")/.."` so they act on the repo root
# whatever directory you invoke them from -- the same idiom the run- wrappers
# use.
/local/
manifests/local/

*.log
*.tmp
*.bak
*.swp
*.swo
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.egg-info/
__pycache__/
.DS*

sample_data/
